    "honest_camp_strength": "Their argument is functionally intuitive: Trynd E + Flash immediately deals Trynd E's own damage, which fits a casual reading of 'landing the skill more in a specific way that is more optimal to deal damage... from that dash ability'.",
    "honest_camp_vulnerability": "The prompt's strange phrasing: it repeatedly uses the technical term 'buffer' ('make use of the buffer', 'ensure that the ability lands more effectively (buffer)', 'buffer dash +Flash'). In League of Legends technical jargon, an input buffer is a specific engine mechanic (queuing a discrete spell/hitbox to resolve on a target). Tryndamere's E has absolutely NO input buffer—it is a continuous moving aura. If the author intended general hitbox relocation, they wouldn't have stressed 'buffer' three separate times and excluded 'repositioning only'.",
    "strategic_framing_for_me": "Position Tryndamere as the classic deliberate distractor of this quiz. I will argue that casual players call Trynd E-Flash a 'dash-flash', but the prompt author deliberately inserted the 'buffer' caveats and '(not for repositioning only)' specifically to test whether test-takers understand the difference between buffered terminal hitboxes (the other 10) and an unbuffered mid-spin translation."
